<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vande Mataram</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">written in the 1870s, probably around <a href="/years/1876">1876</a>; first published <a href="/years/1882">1882</a> in the novel Anandamath</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as বন্দে মাতরম্, Bande Mataram</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Vande Mataram&quot; is a poem written in Bengali, with many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> words, by Bankim Chandra Chatterjee, one of the first graduates of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolkata">Calcutta</a> University, who served the colonial government as a Deputy Collector and later a Deputy Magistrate.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>On 24 January 1950 the Constituent Assembly adopted the first stanza as the national anthem, with &quot;<b>Vande Mataram</b>&quot; honoured equally as the national song.</blockquote><a href="/songs/jana-gana-mana">Jana Gana Mana</a></li><li><blockquote>&quot;<b>Vande Mataram</b>&quot; is a poem written in Bengali, with many Sanskrit words, by Bankim Chandra Chatterjee, one of the first graduates of Calcutta University, who served the colonial government as a Deputy Collector and later a Deputy Magistrate.</blockquote><a href="/songs/vande-mataram">Vande Mataram</a></li></ul></section>
